cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "idtx-flow: the multiplayer-fabric mirror of IDTX Flow"
abstract: >
  IDTX Flow, the Immersive Data Center Management flow tooling, mirrored under this
  organisation with the upstream name kept. The tooling is upstream's and so is its
  README, which carries upstream's own REUSE badge; this copy exists so the fabric can
  pin and patch it. datasource-flow is the diverged sibling that carries the Godot
  integration, and this one stays close to its origin.
authors:
  - name: "Immersive Data Center Management"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/idtx-flow"
keywords:
  - usd
  - gltf
  - godot
  - mirror
references:

  - type: software
    title: "IDTX Flow"
    authors:
      - name: "Immersive Data Center Management"
    url: "https://github.com/Immersive-Data-Center-Management/idtx-flow"
    notes: >
      Upstream, and GitHub carries the fork flag. This is one of five projects whose
      manifest name is not ours to change, because the name on the remote is upstream's
      and renaming it would break the redirect the rest of the world uses.

  - type: software
    title: "REUSE: a specification for licensing and copyright information"
    authors:
      - name: "Free Software Foundation Europe"
    url: "https://reuse.software/"
    notes: >
      Upstream states its licensing through REUSE, which is why this repository carries
      a LICENSES/ directory beside the root LICENSE rather than only one file.
